    "bypass_tpot_floor": 0.95,
    "slope_floor": 0.8,
    "native_layouts": "legal DP/TP/PP/EP and pipeline microbatch layouts",
    "interpolation": "linear TPOT upper bound between the adjacent measured points bracketing the SLO",
    "acceptance": "one fast native run at the best layout's interpolated batch; one above the SLO joins the bracket and the batch is interpolated again, settling at the bracket's passing end within a step of a measured batch; one that proves too big bisects under it; falls back to the best measured passing point",
    "no_rising_line": "double the largest point below the SLO, or halve the smallest above it",
    "beyond_native_reach": "largest measured point, marked limited, never extrapolated",
    "capacity": "bypass KV capacity until a native point reaches it, then native capacity rejections; a KV rejection's reported native capacity batch is measured next",
    "import_speed": "native_stationary_refill_not_always_ready is a too-big point; halving/bisection is reused and the limit is native_import_limited",
    "interval_width": "native_stationary_independent_budget_exceeded is a too-big point; halving/bisection is reused and the limit is native_interval_limited",
    "too_big": "a target at or past the smallest too-big batch bisects from the largest passing point below it, after any reported native capacity below that batch has been tried",
    "wall_projection": "measured wall without the Prefill pass, as measured, against the candidate wall budget; no concurrency divisor",
    "wall_budget": "6 h per candidate and Prefill pass, a guard against a hung worker that must not decide a result: a budget change reuses saved rows, and a row killed under a smaller budget runs again",
    "stopping": "SLO upper-bound bracket; physical capacity, memory and wall limits remain hard limits",
    "pruning": "branch and bound in bypass rate-bound order: the anchor searches from its default first point; later layouts first run where passing the SLO matches the anchor's best passing rate and are pruned when the bypass rate bound (below any native limit, divided by bypass_tpot_floor) or a point above the SLO (rate x (1 + rate_margin)) falls below the case's best measured passing rate, or when a point below the SLO cannot reach it with TPOT growing at slope_floor x min(1, the case's least native/bypass slope ratio from a point within the SLO) x the bypass slope",
    "max_batch": "paper Fig. 3: after the throughput search, the largest per-GPU batch within the SLO by the same branch and bound per layout (bypass batch bound with bypass_tpot_floor, a point above the SLO times 1 + rate_margin, the slope floor), one acceptance run at the best layout's interpolated batch, falling back to the largest measured passing point"
